        "text": "Positive deviation from Raoult's law, for example ethanol + acetone. Dashed lines are the ideal p_A, p_B and p_total; solid curves are the real values. A B interactions are weaker than A A and B B, so both components escape more easily: every curve lies above its Raoult line and ΔH_mix > 0, ΔV_mix > 0."
